  "reply": "`parseDuration` in `src/duration.ts` now accepts the format you described, and `bun test` passes (26 of 26).\n\n- **Accepted input:** one or more components in h, m, s, ms order, with optional whitespace between components and at the ends. No whitespace is allowed between a number and its unit, so `1 s` is rejected, as the existing tests expect.\n- **Rejected input:** empty or blank input, duplicate or out-of-order units, signs, fractions and junk all throw `RangeError`. The input is matched against the whole string, so a partial parse can't succeed.\n- **Overflow:** the total is computed in `BigInt` and checked against `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` before converting back to a number. That catches both a single huge component, like `9007199254740991h`, and a sum that goes over.\n\nThe `parseDuration` export is unchanged, `src/duration.ts` is the only file I edited, and I added no dependencies.",
